# Intent is SELF-HOSTED on v3. Inside this checkout, `intent` must be the v3
# binary -- otherwise the shipped v2 CLI at ~/.local/bin/intent (PATH 17) wins
# and you silently test the wrong product. That shadowing is invisible: v2
# answers `--version` happily and reports 2.19.0 from inside the rewrite.
#
# Scoped deliberately to this directory tree. The fleet's `intent` is v2 and
# must stay v2 -- fifteen projects depend on it -- so this must never be a
# machine-wide PATH change.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO. CORRECTED 2026-08-21 -- dc's find, driven not argued.
# An earlier version of this comment claimed the PATH change ALSO made the
# pre-commit guard bodies resolve from lib/templates/hooks/ HERE instead of from
# the frozen Intentv2 checkout, and called the drift exposure closed. IT IS NOT
# CLOSED. direnv fires at an INTERACTIVE PROMPT; git hooks run non-interactive
# and never see it. Driven in a non-interactive zsh:
#
#   PATH has v3 debug?   0
#   INTENT_HOME          /Users/matts/Devel/prj/Intentv2
#   intent info ->       INTENT_HOME: .../Intentv2   Version: 2.19.0
#   guard runner ->      Intentv2/lib/templates/hooks/pre-commit-guards.sh
#
# AND EVERY NODE HERE COMMITS THROUGH TOOL CALLS, WHICH ARE NON-INTERACTIVE, so
# for this estate the claim was not merely unreliable -- it was inert for every
# commit any of us makes. It covers hv typing `git commit` by hand and nothing
# else. hv had ALREADY DECLINED direnv as the guard-resolution mechanism on
# exactly this ground, in a directive vc was custodian of.
#
# WHY IT GOT THROUGH, BECAUSE THAT IS THE REUSABLE PART: it was framed as a SIDE
# EFFECT. A benefit reclassified as incidental escapes the ruling that governs
# it -- the disclaimer ("this is not the mechanism") is what let the mechanism's
# claimed benefit past. The mechanism assignment is dc's and stays OPEN.
PATH_add "$(expand_path native/rust/target/debug)"
